content:
## Scope

This rule of the Specialty Pharmacy Program sets the **maximizer program draw**: the payment a manufacturer program makes, under a maximizer program, on the latest shipped fill of a specialty enrollment. It does not cover:

- enrollments whose program coordinates assistance by standard coordination or by variable copay;
- a member whose plan backs assisted amounts out of the accumulators.

The draw is recorded against the program name and the program year of the latest benefit load. It pays the fill's deductible portion first, and the part that covers that deductible portion is recorded as the draw's deductible portion.

## What booking the draw does

Booking a maximizer program draw on one shipped fill:

- records the assistance applied, together with the part of it that pays the fill's deductible portion, not backed out of the plan accumulators;
- posts the matching payment from the manufacturer program against the same fill;
- lowers the enrollment's remaining manufacturer assistance by the amount;
- lowers the member's balance due on the enrollment by the same amount.

Afterwards the fill shows the maximizer program draw in the enrollment's assistance and payment history, and the member owes that much less.

## How it is invoked

The action is `apply_maximizer_draw_3be5be4a`, an agent-side tool. The agent unlocks it and then calls it.

## Parameters

| Parameter | Meaning | Format |
|---|---|---|
| `specialty_enrollment_id` | Reference number of the member's specialty therapy enrollment the fill belongs to, as read from the specialty enrollment lookup | Identifier |
| `specialty_fill_id` | Reference number of the shipped fill the program draw is applied to, as read from the specialty fill lookup. It is a shipment entry, not a scheduled one. | Identifier |
| `program_name` | Name of the manufacturer program exactly as it appears on the program's benefit load entry in the enrollment's assistance history | Verbatim: copied character for character, with no translation, normalisation, summarising, addition or deletion |
| `program_year` | Program year of the benefit being drawn on, exactly as on that benefit load entry | Four-digit year, YYYY |
| `amount` | The program draw applied to the fill | USD, a positive amount to 2 decimal places (nearest cent) |
| `deductible_portion` | The part of the program draw that pays the fill's deductible portion | USD to 2 decimal places; 0.00 when none of it pays a deductible portion |

## Return

On success the receipt contains:

- `status`: "applied";
- `assistance_entry_id`: reference number of the assistance-applied entry;
- `payment_entry_id`: reference number of the matching manufacturer-program payment entry;
- `specialty_fill_id`: the fill paid;
- `amount`: the draw booked, in USD to 2 decimal places;
- `assistance_balance`: the enrollment's remaining manufacturer assistance after the booking, in USD to 2 decimal places;
- `balance_due`: the member's balance due on the enrollment after the booking, in USD to 2 decimal places.
